<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR firms to 12.13 from 12.09 pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR firms to 12.13 from 12.09 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month rose to 12.13 from 12.09 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) edged up to 11.64 from 11.60 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Feb  13  12.13   12.01   11.04   11.64   11.53   11.46</p>
<p> Feb  12  12.09   11.98   11.83   11.63   11.56   11.46</p>
<p> Feb  11  12.09   11.99   11.84   11.67   11.57   11.49</p>
<p> Feb  07  12.10   12.00   11.88   11.68   11.57   11.50</p>
<p> Feb  04  12.13   12.01   11.88   11.68   11.57   11.50</p>
<p> Jan  31  12.20   12.08   11.91   11.73   11.63   11.55</p>
<p> Jan  30  12.19   12.09   11.91   11.73   11.62   11.56</p>
<p> Jan  29  12.19   12.09   11.92   11.73   11.63   11.56</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Feb  13  11.64   11.52   11.35   11.15   11.04   10.98</p>
<p> Feb  12  11.60   11.49   11.34   11.14   11.06   10.97</p>
<p> Feb  11  11.60   11.50   11.35   11.17   11.08   11.00</p>
<p> Feb  07  11.61   11.50   11.38   11.17   11.07   11.00</p>
<p> Feb  04  11.64   11.52   11.38   11.18   11.07   11.00</p>
<p> Jan  31  11.70   11.58   11.41   11.23   11.12   11.04</p>
<p> Jan  30  11.69   11.59   11.41   11.23   11.12   11.06</p>
<p> Jan  29  11.69   11.59   11.42   11.23   11.13   11.06</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 18 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
